    <node id="Lardoel Campus">
      <data key="d0">Lardoel Campus</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Lardoel Campus is a key geographic location and operational hub of Zastama Industries. It serves as a central site for a wide range of functions, including research, development, administrative operations, and critical IT infrastructure. The campus opened in 2013 and has since played a vital role in the company's infrastructure ecosystem, particularly in the areas of data routing, redundancy, and high-availability systems.

Several important systems and projects are hosted at Lardoel Campus, including the Hunbenan Beacon, the Tusgagiel Ledger, the Ketemram Vault, and the Krorhitra Console. The Tusgagiel Ledger, in particular, is configured to meet stringent security and availability requirements. The campus also supports cross-departmental initiatives and has been involved in collaboration with the Genfinel Platform Group, which is based there. It is also expected to be represented in the task force for the Garelor Relay infrastructure review.

The campus has a capacity for 320 seats and is the primary site for the coordination and integration of Puzeris Systems' equipment. It is a location where multiple individuals are based, including Drikres Tikrais, a UX Researcher; Kavemen Hilister, who contributes to engineering, development, and coordination efforts, including Project Lovulett; and Sotroa Veriris, who is involved in research and administrative functions. Additional personnel such as Fongois Bakemdia, Novoran Trabrelor, and Vosaett Neldelis are also based at the site. Recent improvements, including the delivery of new equipment, have further enhanced the campus's operational capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A location serving as a hub for innovation and collaboration at Zastama Industries, where cross-functional teams work on key initiatives such as the Bankis Compass, Project Vatuen, and Project Minkegais.</data>
