    <node id="Pozoine Campus">
      <data key="d0">Pozoine Campus</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Pozoine Campus is an operational site of Zastama Industries, located in the northern region and serving as a central hub for various departments, teams, and key personnel. It opened in 2018 and is managed by Bedras Sarkua, who is also based there. The campus has a capacity for 580 seats and is focused on financial performance, resource allocation, and data-driven decision-making. It functions within expected performance metrics and plays a critical role in the company's infrastructure operations.

The Pozoine Campus hosts several critical systems and facilities, including the Samopunel Beacon and the Natrala Relay, both of which are essential to Zastama Industries' operations. It is also the location where the Vesterge Ledger is hosted. The campus supports inter-campus coordination and serves as the base for the Drurlomis Integration Team and the Drugoan Platform Group, facilitating close collaboration between these teams. As a central hub, it is integral to the strategic and operational activities of Zastama Industries.&lt;SEP&gt;A location where infrastructure components are being deployed and where Talgal Trozien is based.&lt;SEP&gt;A location where Benvuze Vonumanor is based and where innovation and infrastructure strategy advancements are being led.&lt;SEP&gt;A geographic location that hosts the Zathunel Beacon and provides infrastructure for the Sabrinett Analytics Unit.</data>
