    <node id="Master Services Agreement">
      <data key="d0">Master Services Agreement</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Master Services Agreement is a contractual framework used by Zastama Industries to formalize long-term engagements with various service providers. These agreements typically outline the scope of services, duration, and key performance terms. One such agreement is a 12-month contract under which Stevosdim Partners provides component delivery and system integration services for the Hunbenan Beacon. Another 12-month agreement involves Pengamine Consulting, which is engaged to provide strategic consultation. 

Zastama Industries also has an 18-month Master Services Agreement with Mepoen Consulting for advisory support. A separate 18-month agreement is in place with Hurpuman Partners, which outlines the terms of the services provided and is set for renewal in Q4 FY26. Additionally, Zastama Industries has an 18-month contract with Nusnila Systems for Project Drosvais, and a 36-month agreement with Krolpumen Labs, which outlines service milestones and integration activities. 

Another Master Services Agreement is a contractual agreement between Zastama Industries and Nedroran Fabrication, scheduled to expire at the end of FY27 and up for renewal in Q1 FY28. These agreements collectively reflect Zastama Industries’ strategic approach to managing long-term service engagements across multiple partners and projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-001-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-049-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-019-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-021-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-027-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-014-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-036-chunk-000</data>
