    <node id="Predictive Maintenance">
      <data key="d0">Predictive Maintenance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A system introduced through fleet telemetry that allows for more accurate tracking and maintenance planning, reducing downtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive Maintenance is a method that could be applied to large-scale initiatives like Project Serinen and Project Medeis. It involves using real-time processing and anomaly detection models to anticipate and prevent system failures.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive maintenance is a strategy that uses data analysis to predict when maintenance should be performed. It is a key area of research for the Daslaor Applied Research Lab and relevant to Project Medeis.&lt;SEP&gt;A maintenance strategy that uses data analysis to predict when equipment maintenance is needed. Initial pilot tests in this area have shown promising results.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive Maintenance is a method used in the Kavafa Systems contract to anticipate and prevent equipment failures based on telemetry data.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategy used by Zastama Industries to anticipate and prevent equipment failures by analyzing telemetry data.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-038-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-084-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-046-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-057-chunk-000</data>
