    <node id="Procurement">
      <data key="d0">Procurement</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of acquiring materials and services, overseen by the Procurement Manager to ensure supply chain efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;A process managed by Dronoan Bolgesan for acquiring specialized hardware and licensing agreements for Project Tinpia. It includes coordinating with vendors, negotiating terms, and maintaining transparency with stakeholders.&lt;SEP&gt;Procurement is a department represented in the cross-functional workshops and is part of the operational teams involved in implementing adjustments based on forecasting models.&lt;SEP&gt;A department or function involved in managing procurement orders and vendor contracts for both Project Kososett and Project Dernelnar.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of acquiring new data retention tools or services.&lt;SEP&gt;A business process involving the acquisition of goods or services, as discussed in the email exchanges between Thuszus Kustoen and Zondila Krerraris.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-009-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-024-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-012-chunk-000</data>
