    <node id="Vendor Contracts">
      <data key="d0">Vendor Contracts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal agreements between Zastama Industries and its vendors, currently undergoing review for clarity and risk mitigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal agreements in place for the procurement of components for Project Krabehien.&lt;SEP&gt;Vendor Contracts are agreements between Zastama Industries and external vendors for the provision of goods or services, particularly relevant to Project Kososett during its planning phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Contracts related to the Lorhia Loom that are being reviewed for documentation gaps.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal agreements between the Stonfe Analytics Unit and external vendors for software licenses and tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal agreements being reviewed by Zastama Industries to ensure resource availability and alignment with the final phase of Project Komsonor.&lt;SEP&gt;Agreements between the organization and external vendors for services related to Project Sankonen.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-011-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-044-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-031-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-016-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-011&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-044&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-005&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-031&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-016&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-023</data>
      <data key="d5">1793686539</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fongois Bakemdia">
      <data key="d0">Fongois Bakemdia</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Fongois Bakemdia is a person who works at the Lardoel Campus and is responsible for coordinating with Puzeris Systems and overseeing the renewal discussions for their contract. They also report to no one explicitly in the text but are the sender of the initial email update.&lt;SEP&gt;A team member at Zastama Industries who supports Zevus Lokramel’s initiatives and has been instrumental in establishing processes for faster deployment of response tools and better coordination between product and operations teams.&lt;SEP&gt;Fongois Bakemdia is an individual who attended the Q2 Strategic Review and Operational Planning Meeting. He is based at the Lardoel Campus and provided an overview of recent updates to internal systems used in the customer onboarding process.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-104-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-010&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-104</data>
      <data key="d5">1793666005</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Zevus Lokramel">
      <data key="d0">Zevus Lokramel</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Zevus Lokramel is a person who reports to Fongois Bakemdia and is involved in coordinating with Puzeris Systems, particularly in ensuring the delivery and maintenance of their equipment align with the needs of the Lardoel Campus. They also coordinate with internal teams and the vendor for renewal discussions.&lt;SEP&gt;A representative who presented an overview of incident response tooling initiatives, including improvements in system monitoring and escalation protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;A Product Manager and project lead for Project Zelpan, responsible for bridging technical and legal considerations since 2017.&lt;SEP&gt;A professional at Zastama Industries who focuses on incident response tooling and works on refining tools to detect and mitigate system anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;A key member of the Drugoan Platform Group who focuses on incident response tooling. Zevus Lokramel develops and maintains the tools used by the team to detect, respond to, and resolve system incidents.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-025-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-039-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-086-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-010&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-025&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-039&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-086</data>
      <data key="d5">1793663695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kragura Stenmori">
      <data key="d0">Kragura Stenmori</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Kragura Stenmori is a person based at the Lardoel Campus and plays a key role in overseeing the integration of Puzeris Systems' equipment into the campus operations. They work closely with the vendor to resolve operational challenges and prepare reports for renewal evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;The person actively managing day-to-day execution of Project Tinpia and coordinating with cross-functional teams.&lt;SEP&gt;A key member of the workforce at Zastama Industries, based at the Lardoel Campus.&lt;SEP&gt;The direct supervisor of Pethisa Hebroren, providing strategic direction and oversight for data retention tooling.&lt;SEP&gt;A Research Lead at Zastama Industries who requires physical access to a secure vault for material analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-016-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-041-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-024-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-010&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-016&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-041&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-013&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-024</data>
      <data key="d5">1793686516</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Puzeris Systems">
      <data key="d0">Puzeris Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Puzeris Systems is an organization that provides equipment and services to the Lardoel Campus. They have a contract worth $5.9M and are involved in the renewal discussions for FY27. Their equipment supports the 320-seat environment at the campus.&lt;SEP&gt;A key vendor in Zastama Industries' supply chain, supplying components for the Sallama Lattice. They are instrumental in ensuring the performance and reliability of the lattice and are engaged in long-term maintenance and upgrade planning.&lt;SEP&gt;An external partner providing infrastructure and maintenance support for Project Golgoett.&lt;SEP&gt;Puzeris Systems is an organization providing services for Project Golgoett. It is being evaluated for potential cross-project support and shared infrastructure opportunities with Kosnaren Systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Puzeris Systems is a vendor providing services for Project Golgoett. The collaboration with this organization has been smooth, and regular check-ins are being maintained to ensure alignment with project goals.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization contracted to provide security integration services for Project Golgoett. They are working with the Vurlekri Annex team.&lt;SEP&gt;A supplier of critical components for the Sallama Lattice, involved in maintaining the platform's performance and reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-053-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-058-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-085-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-055-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-110-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-010&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-051&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-053&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-058&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-085&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-055&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-110</data>
      <data key="d5">1793696083</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Project Golgoett">
      <data key="d0">Project Golgoett</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Project Golgoett is an internal initiative at Zastama Industries, primarily focused on the development and integration of a critical internal platform. The project is owned by the Zugula Infrastructure Team and is staffed by 10 individuals, directly supervised by Ragos Drosporel. It operates under budget code EY-4267-K and cost center MN-8713-X, with strict access governance in place to maintain the integrity of its core tools and data. The initiative is currently in a stable development phase with no compliance concerns and is on track to meet its interim milestones.

A key aspect of Project Golgoett is its services contract with Puzeris Systems, which provides external support in infrastructure and maintenance. The renewal of this contract is being evaluated in the context of the project's strategic goals and operational requirements for FY27. Additionally, the project is being considered for potential synergies with Project Vumzosa to reduce costs and improve resource efficiency. The vendor team has been delivering key components as scheduled, and the project is progressing according to plan.

However, an audit has identified discrepancies in the documentation of personnel time logs and resource usage, raising concerns about the accuracy of project reporting. Despite this, the initiative remains a key focus within the engineering division and is central to enhancing the resilience and scalability of Zastama Industries' network architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;An ongoing project focused on the integration of identity and access tooling. It involves multiple teams and organizations working together to ensure a smooth deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-053-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-058-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-085-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-108-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-050-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-055-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-010&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-023&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-053&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-058&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-085&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-108&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-006&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-005&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-050&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-055</data>
      <data key="d5">1793694834</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="$5.9M">
      <data key="d0">$5.9M</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">$5.9M is the monetary value of the contract between the Lardoel Campus and Puzeris Systems for the delivery and maintenance of equipment.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-010-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-010</data>
      <data key="d5">1793655154</data>
