    <node id="Finance Team">
      <data key="d0">Finance Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Finance Team is a department within Zastama Industries responsible for a wide range of financial oversight, budget management, and compliance-related activities. They play a central role in managing budget allocations, ensuring financial transparency, and supporting strategic priorities across various projects and departments. The team collaborates closely with multiple internal stakeholders, including the project lead for Nedroran Fabrication, the product team for the Vesterge Ledger, and the Procurement Team for reconciliation reports and procurement order processing. They are involved in reviewing and processing procurement requests, including Procurement Order QK-5662-N, and are responsible for approving and finalizing procurement orders while ensuring compliance with internal controls and financial parameters.

The Finance Team manages access permissions for finance-related roles and reviews the financial terms of contracts and services agreements, such as the one with Krolpumen Labs. They support various projects by providing budgetary analysis and resource planning, including Project Barkil, Project Vumzosa, the Lorhia Loom, and Project Tukrama. The team is also involved in capital allocation decisions and invited to strategic planning sessions to discuss long-term support and maintenance strategies. They monitor expenditures for projects such as Project Brasti, Braveor Fabrication, Project Stepoen, and Project Nondaran, ensuring that spending remains within approved limits and that documentation is up to date.

In addition, the Finance Team is responsible for financial reporting, audit integration, and maintaining compliance with internal controls. They conduct audits, review cost centers and contracts, and ensure that financial records are accurate and current. They monitor payment schedules, fulfill contractual obligations, and verify the accuracy of budget codes and cost centers for external partners such as Bekuine Consulting and Radesan Consulting. The Finance Team is also involved in ongoing discussions to clarify contractual terms and ensure compliance with internal and external regulatory requirements for Project Medeis.

The team is responsible for confirming funding and contractual status for vendor agreements and monitoring the financial aspects of the engagement with Mortalis Consulting to ensure spending aligns with projections. They are involved in reviewing the audit findings and considering possible reallocation of resources for the Lozeine Applied Research Lab. The Finance Team also oversees budget constraints for projects such as Project Sankonen and Project Krindais, ensuring alignment with financial projections and organizational goals. Overall, the Finance Team serves as a critical internal function at Zastama Industries, ensuring that financial resources are managed effectively, compliance is maintained, and projects remain aligned with organizational goals and financial constraints.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-012-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-043-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-058-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-085-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-018-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-025-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-034-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-046-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-057-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-059-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-016-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-022-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-024-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-036-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-040-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-043-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-001-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-031-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-036-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-034-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-044-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-050-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-058-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-035-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-007-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-034-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-049-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-021-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-037-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-070-chunk-000</data>
