    <node id="Transparency">
      <data key="d0">Transparency</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency is a core cultural and operational principle emphasized across multiple departments and projects within Zastama Industries. It is described as a key component of the company's culture and strategic direction, fostered by leadership and various department heads, including the Finance Lead and Operations Director. Transparency is promoted through open communication, information sharing, and understanding of the organizational structure and key projects. It is also emphasized in periodic status reports and internal processes, aiming to ensure alignment across stakeholders and maintain an environment of accountability.

At the project level, Transparency is maintained in procurement activities, vendor-related operations, and financial reporting. It is particularly emphasized in the management of contracts such as the Zitrien Partners agreement and the Kusbosine Console, where clear and accessible budget and cost data are prioritized. In Project Tinpia and Project Ruzonine, transparency involves keeping stakeholders informed about procurement progress and ensuring accountability through oversight and reconciliation details. The principle is also a goal of procurement and escrow actions, where openness in internal processes is actively pursued.

Overall, Transparency is consistently portrayed as a foundational value at Zastama Industries, supported by multiple leaders and integrated into both strategic and operational practices. It is seen as essential for fostering trust, accountability, and effective communication across all levels of the organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-014-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-016-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-032-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-031-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-043-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-078-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-113-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-030-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-047-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-003-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-023-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-059-chunk-000</data>
