    </node>
    <node id="Dronoan Bolgesan">
      <data key="d0">Dronoan Bolgesan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The Procurement Manager at Zastama Industries, responsible for managing the acquisition of specialized hardware and licensing agreements for Project Tinpia. Dronoan Bolgesan ensures that all necessary resources are secured on time and within budget, and works closely with Broteor Pikrisen's team to align procurement timelines with project milestones.&lt;SEP&gt;A member of the finance department at Zastama Industries whose role in payments reconciliation relies on secure and user-friendly systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Dronoan Bolgesan is a Procurement Manager who has been a valued part of the company since 2022. They are responsible for payments reconciliation and have contributed significantly to streamlining vendor interactions and improving internal reporting accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-064-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-085-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-013&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-064&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-085</data>
      <data key="d5">1793663615</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Zondila Krerraris">
      <data key="d0">Zondila Krerraris</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An employee at Zastama Industries since 2017. Zondila Krerraris has contributed significantly to past initiatives and has collaborated closely with Broteor Pikrisen on several phases of Project Tinpia, providing valuable insights into system architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;A key member of the Somhoine Risk Office, instrumental in coordinating stakeholder input and ensuring risk parameters align with the company's strategic objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Procurement Manager coordinating vault access and procurement items for Project Renbomen.&lt;SEP&gt;Zondila Krerraris is a project leader involved in Project Laguran and is responsible for coordinating with the finance representative to finalize escrow documentation. She also provides updates on team structure and user experience improvements for Zasdaett Harbor.&lt;SEP&gt;A person responsible for managing a procurement order and contract for Zastama Industries. They provide updates on deliverables and confirm the status of contractual obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;Zondila Krerraris is a Procurement Manager who works closely with Krosso Velfosan to confirm that procurement documentation is compiled and available for review. She has arranged meetings to address discrepancies and has reviewed procurement protocols in light of new onboarding procedures. She has also recommended maintaining coordination as a standard practice.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-072-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-008-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-030-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-012-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-023-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-013&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-072&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-008&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-030&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-012&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-023</data>
      <data key="d5">1793758715</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="System Reliability">
      <data key="d0">System Reliability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A focus area of Project Tinpia, referring to the ability of systems to perform consistently and without failure over time.&lt;SEP&gt;An expected outcome of Project Tinpia. It refers to the ability of systems to perform consistently and without failure after the project is completed.&lt;SEP&gt;The consistent and dependable operation of the Femfasel Vault, which has not been impacted by reported performance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;System Reliability refers to the ability of a system to perform consistently and without failure. It is a key objective of Project Lovulett.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-040-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-083-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-013&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-040&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-083</data>
      <data key="d5">1793695719</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
