      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Milestone">
      <data key="d0">Milestone</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A key point in the timeline of Project Tinpia. Broteor Pikrisen is responsible for defining these milestones, and Dronoan Bolgesan ensures procurement timelines align with them.&lt;SEP&gt;A key achievement or target in the timeline of Project Pomtorgi, expected to be met in the coming weeks.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-034-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-013&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-034</data>
      <data key="d5">1793759058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Timeline">
      <data key="d0">Timeline</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A schedule managed by Dronoan Bolgesan and aligned with project milestones for Project Tinpia. It ensures that resources are secured on time.&lt;SEP&gt;Timeline refers to the schedule or sequence of events for the coordination session and related activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The schedule for Project Barkil, to be updated and submitted by Munnam Furzil and Konalis Thisfol by May 31, 2026.&lt;SEP&gt;The schedule outlining the planned delivery and integration of the equipment at the Gahikron Campus.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-061-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-088-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-032-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-030-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-013&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-088&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-032&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-030</data>
      <data key="d5">1793692684</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vendor Coordination">
      <data key="d0">Vendor Coordination</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A process managed by Dronoan Bolgesan for Project Tinpia. It involves working with external vendors to secure necessary resources.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of working with external vendors, such as Gibasan Logistics, to ensure timely and compliant delivery of project components.&lt;SEP&gt;Vendor coordination refers to the management and collaboration with external vendors to ensure timely and effective project execution. In this context, it is a key focus area for Project Nondaran.</data>
