    </node>
    <node id="Product Development">
      <data key="d0">Product Development</data>
      <data key="d1">department</data>
      <data key="d2">A department within Zastama Industries involved in the development and implementation of projects such as Project Dramen.&lt;SEP&gt;A department at Zastama Industries responsible for guiding the development of new products and ensuring alignment with company objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;A process within Zastama Industries involving the planning, design, and implementation of new or improved products. It was a central topic of the meeting.&lt;SEP&gt;A departmental activity at Zastama Industries focused on aligning feature roadmaps with user feedback and resolving bottlenecks in the testing phase.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-005-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-055-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-005&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-055</data>
      <data key="d5">1793692684</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Working Group">
      <data key="d0">Working Group</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Working Group is a term used to describe multiple newly established or proposed teams within Zastama Industries and other related projects, each with distinct objectives and compositions. These groups are typically formed to address specific strategic, operational, or compliance-related challenges. One such group is tasked with overseeing the next steps of Project Dramen and providing regular updates to the executive team. Another is being proposed to explore synergies between Project Medeis and other initiatives, particularly in the areas of predictive modeling and fleet behavior analysis.

A separate working group is being proposed to address integration challenges for Project Vatuen, led by Sotroa Veriris. Another group has been established to oversee the integration of warehouse automation systems with existing infrastructure. Additionally, a proposed group aims to assess and enhance interdepartmental collaboration, identified as a key action item from a recent meeting. Another team is being formed to assess the long-term viability of process improvements and identify potential limitations.

A group has also been established to evaluate potential integrations for the payments reconciliation process. At Zastama Industries, a newly formed Working Group consists of representatives from engineering and compliance, tasked with drafting a remediation plan for an audit finding. Another group, composed of members from security, compliance, and product engineering teams, is formed to assist in finalizing the rollout plan for identity and access enhancements.

A team has been assembled to evaluate the technical feasibility and user impact of proposed enhancements to the Zasdaett Harbor. Another group is tasked with drafting recommendations on how escrow-related transactions are integrated with broader financial systems. A proposed group is intended to facilitate the transition from infrastructure to operations, led by Rozor Habanis and including Ragos Drosporel and an operations team representative.

At Zastama Industries, a newly formed group comprising the Project Lead (Project Laguran), Senior Program Manager, and Finance Representative is exploring cross-project synergies and resource optimization. Another team has been formed to evaluate the broader implications of vendor access at the Gahikron Campus, including security protocols. Finally, a group at Zastama Industries is currently reviewing proposed timelines for the next phase of integration with Zosu Kistos.&lt;SEP&gt;A group to be formed and led by the IT representative to assess the scalability of the Brapoett Vault.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-096-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-103-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-112-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-041-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-006-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-031-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-038-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-052-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-055-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-014-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-050-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-021-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-017&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-042&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-073&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-096&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-103&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-112&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-041&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-006&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-031&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-038&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-051&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-052&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-055&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-014&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-050&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-021</data>
      <data key="d5">1793693604</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Executive Team">
      <data key="d0">Executive Team</data>
      <data key="d1">team</data>
      <data key="d2">The Executive Team is the senior leadership group at Zastama Industries responsible for overseeing and guiding major organizational initiatives and projects. This team is tasked with receiving regular status updates and detailed reports on various projects, including Project Daslalett, Project Stukoett, Project Drugilett, Project Nondaran, and the Zartesis Prism. These updates are typically submitted following the Strategic Planning and Operational Review Meeting, ensuring that the Executive Team remains informed on progress, risks, and strategic alignment.

Members of the Executive Team are involved in reviewing revised timelines, contingency plans, and integration testing outcomes for projects under their purview. For instance, they have reviewed the revised timeline and contingency plan for Project Drugilett and are expected to conduct a final review of Project Komsonor after the completion of integration testing and validation. Additionally, Pinhan Bilfael is required to report on the progress of Project Stukoett to this leadership group.

The Executive Team plays a central role in monitoring and guiding high-priority initiatives such as Project Dramen, ensuring that strategic objectives are met and that any emerging risks are promptly addressed. Their oversight contributes to the overall direction and success of Zastama Industries' key projects and long-term goals.&lt;SEP&gt;The senior leadership team of Zastama Industries that receives regular status updates on Project Krindais.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-017-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-033-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-105-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-115-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-118-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-025-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-036-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-002-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-047-chunk-000</data>
