      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vambi Herganen">
      <data key="d0">Vambi Herganen</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Vambi Herganen is a prominent professional at Zastama Industries, currently serving as Chief of Staff with a primary focus on fleet telemetry. Since joining the company in 2021, Herganen has played a crucial role in strengthening data operations and has significantly enhanced the reliability and performance of telemetry systems. In this capacity, Herganen is responsible for overseeing and optimizing the collection and analysis of data from vehicle fleets, contributing to operational efficiency and decision-making processes.

In addition to their role in fleet telemetry, Vambi Herganen leads the Lozeine Applied Research Lab, where they are responsible for driving innovation and supporting Zastama Industries' broader innovation strategy. Herganen provides regular updates on applied research initiatives and has led the formation of a strategic working group and a communication plan to align research efforts with organizational goals. The lab is also involved in developing scalable solutions and facilitating discussions between the Lardoel Campus and the research group, ensuring cross-functional collaboration and knowledge sharing.

Herganen is actively involved in several key projects, including Project Ralamel, where they contribute to strategic direction and coordination, and Project Monnoheor, with which they have confirmed collaboration. They also provide technical insights and alternative pathways for Project Drugilett, demonstrating their role as a key contributor to the development of multiple initiatives through research and innovation. As a central figure in both operational and research domains, Vambi Herganen plays a vital role in advancing Zastama Industries' technological and strategic objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;A Chief of Staff at Zastama Industries who also leads the Lozeine Applied Research Lab.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-024-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-043-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-046-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-063-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-107-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-114-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-115-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-057-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-089-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-024&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-043&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-046&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-063&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-107&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-114&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-115&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-057&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-089</data>
      <data key="d5">1793695946</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Project Hamuis">
      <data key="d0">Project Hamuis</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An initiative within Zastama Industries that is being developed in coordination with Project Ralamel and is built on the Brenian Console.&lt;SEP&gt;A project owned by the Drurlomis Integration Team that is at an exciting stage of development and is expected to contribute to the company’s strategic goals.&lt;SEP&gt;A project currently in a stable phase of execution, aligned with the strategic goals of Zastama Industries, and focused on refining technical specifications and coordinating external testing protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;A project that is progressing as planned, having completed the second phase of development and entering the implementation stage. It is staffed by 31 people.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical project at Zastama Industries built on the Brenian Console, currently in the second phase of its integration framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-024-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-074-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-007-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-054-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-081-chunk-000</data>
