    <node id="Thamhuor Campus">
      <data key="d0">Thamhuor Campus</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Thamhuor Campus is a physical and operational location of Zastama Industries, situated in the eastern region of the company’s operations. It has been in use since 2013 and serves as a key site for multiple departments, supporting on-site coordination, system maintenance, and interdepartmental communication. The campus operates at near capacity and is integral to the company’s strategic direction and development initiatives.

Thamhuor Campus is the primary base for the Zugula Infrastructure Team, which manages infrastructure-related projects and initiatives from this location. It is also where Fakra Sermus and their team have provided technical and operational support for the Tanumett Relay, and where infrastructure upgrades are being conducted to support broader Zastama Industries initiatives. Additionally, Dreto Zampusrar is based at the campus, which has seen increased activity due to the expansion of several key projects.

The campus is a designated site for the delivery of equipment for Project Drannen by Nerasan Labs and is the primary location for the next phase of field testing for Project Loloman, as well as for the installation of Nerasan Labs equipment. It has also hosted interdepartmental meetings, underscoring its role as a central hub for collaboration and operational alignment within Zastama Industries.&lt;SEP&gt;Thamhuor Campus is a critical site for Zastama Industries where equipment is being delivered by Hurpuman Partners. It is the location of several ongoing initiatives and is involved in on-site coordination of deliveries.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-028-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-048-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-062-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-064-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-066-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-071-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-080-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-114-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-118-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-036-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-028&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-045&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-048&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-062&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-064&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-066&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-071&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-080&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-114&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-118&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-036</data>
      <data key="d5">1793757448</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Data Retention Tooling">
      <data key="d0">Data Retention Tooling</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Retention Tooling refers to a set of systems and tools designed to manage the retention, archiving, retrieval, and deletion of data in compliance with regulatory requirements while ensuring its accessibility for analytical and operational purposes. These tools are critical for maintaining data integrity and supporting long-term data governance strategies within organizations.

The development and refinement of Data Retention Tooling are being led by multiple contributors. The Fozola Applied Research Lab is currently working on a set of tools in the stabilization phase. Additionally, Kestoen Pismiett is leading a system or software initiative aimed at enhancing data handling processes within regulatory boundaries, specifically to support Zastama Industries' data governance strategy. Bonosun Torpesan has also contributed to the development of tools that improve Zastama Industries' ability to maintain and utilize high-quality data. Pethisa Hebroren is involved in integrating similar tooling as a necessary component for the long-term viability of Project Komsonor.

Currently, the Data Retention Tooling used by Zastama Industries is functional but has notable limitations, such as the absence of audit trails and metadata tagging. These tools are intended to ensure that data is retained in a structured and compliant manner, supporting both operational needs and regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-028-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-076-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-041-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-020-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-017-chunk-000</data>
