    <node id="Identity and Access Tooling">
      <data key="d0">Identity and Access Tooling</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Identity and Access Tooling refers to the systems, software, and procedures designed to manage user identities, authentication, authorization, and access control. These tools are essential for maintaining security, compliance, and efficient user management within infrastructure systems. At Zastama Industries, Identity and Access Tooling is a key focus area, with efforts underway to enhance security, streamline onboarding, and improve user permissions across internal systems. Thegen Zilkanett has contributed to improving the user experience of these tools, reflecting a broader initiative to make access management more intuitive and secure. The tooling is also being upgraded to support Project Monnoheor’s internal systems, emphasizing its role in securing access to sensitive operations. Overall, Identity and Access Tooling serves as a critical component in ensuring both system integrity and user convenience.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of tools related to identity and access management, requested for infrastructure upgrades at the Brokamis Campus.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-030-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-061-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-064-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-088-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-101-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-119-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-083-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-097-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-032-chunk-000</data>
