    </node>
    <node id="Cross-Functional Teams">
      <data key="d0">Cross-Functional Teams</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cross-Functional Teams are groups composed of members from different departments or functions within Zastama Industries. These teams are formed to enhance collaboration and efficiency by bringing together diverse expertise to address complex organizational challenges. They work across departments to ensure that documentation, procurement, and data retention processes align with both technical and regulatory requirements. In particular, Dopusa Varesett serves as a key point of contact for these teams, especially in the area of telemetry data integration.

Cross-Functional Teams are involved in the coordination and execution of various projects, including Project Stukoett, Project Sankonen, and Project Hinzosine. They also collaborate with Kesonan Mufashua to address challenges related to budget adherence and timeline expectations for Project Medeis. Additionally, these teams assess the impact of the Hurpuman Partners renewal process and work closely with external and internal stakeholders, such as the Thanfuan Applied Research Lab and the Trehaett Applied Research Lab, to ensure that products like the Maslarine Compass and the Samopunel Beacon meet technical, operational, and customer expectations. Their work is further supported by collaboration with Nosos Nikeis to maintain alignment with organizational standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Teams composed of members from different departments or areas of expertise, working together on key initiatives at Zastama Industries.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-073-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-078-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-024-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-020-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-034-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-053-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-036-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-082-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-099-chunk-000</data>
