    <node id="Project Serinen">
      <data key="d0">Project Serinen</data>
      <data key="d1">project</data>
      <data key="d2">Project Serinen is a large-scale initiative at Zastama Industries that is staffed by 40 people. It is being considered for potential integration with telemetry systems and data science models.&lt;SEP&gt;A central innovation project at Zastama Industries focused on the development and refinement of fleet telemetry systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An ongoing project with a $2.5M budget, staffed by 40 people, and on track to meet its Q2 FY28 completion target. It is a high-visibility initiative.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-038-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-087-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-103-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-038&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-087&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-103</data>
      <data key="d5">1793665828</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Project Medeis">
      <data key="d0">Project Medeis</data>
      <data key="d1">project</data>
      <data key="d2">Project Medeis is a large-scale initiative at Zastama Industries that is staffed by 25 people. It is being considered for potential integration with telemetry systems and data science models.&lt;SEP&gt;Project Medeis is a pilot project with an approved budget of $2.7M, focused on integrating telemetry data to support operational goals. It is in the early stages of implementation and involves collaboration across departments.&lt;SEP&gt;Project Medeis is a key initiative at Zastama Industries. It is on schedule to meet its Q2 FY27 completion target, with several key milestones already achieved. The project team is working closely with cross-functional partners to ensure all technical and regulatory requirements are being met.&lt;SEP&gt;A project owned by the Zizadal Infrastructure Team, currently on track for Q2 FY27 completion. It involves infrastructure development and is being reviewed for alignment with industry standards and financial projections.&lt;SEP&gt;Project Medeis is a high-priority initiative focused on enhancing data flow and system resilience. It involves redundancy protocols, migration strategies, and compliance reviews to ensure system stability and security.&lt;SEP&gt;Project Medeis is a critical initiative within the department, operating under cost center TC-7832-A and governed by contract number YY-9419-Y. It is currently in a phase of strategic review and financial recalibration.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-038-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-045-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-052-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-056-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-034-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-038&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-042&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-045&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-052&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-056&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-034</data>
      <data key="d5">1793698105</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
