      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Daslaor Applied Research Lab">
      <data key="d0">Daslaor Applied Research Lab</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Daslaor Applied Research Lab is a research organization within Zastama Industries, based at the Vurlekri Annex, and headed by Votirmi Tresbior. It employs 20 individuals who engage in advanced technology development and applied scientific investigation. The lab plays a central role in the company’s research and development efforts, focusing on long-term initiatives through applied research.

The lab conducts research in several key areas, including predictive maintenance, fleet telemetry, data transmission efficiency, and environmental monitoring. It is also actively involved in investigating new methods for predictive modeling in supply chain optimization and exploring opportunities for external collaboration. These efforts are aligned with infrastructure needs and support high-priority projects.

Daslaor Applied Research Lab oversees the execution of multiple projects, including Project Vumzosa, Project Minkegais, Project Statugoan, and Project Tholgu. It provides updates on these initiatives during the Strategic Planning and Operational Review Meeting and plays a role in decision-making processes related to contract renewals, resource allocation, and cross-project synergies. Krodaor Thaborine, a member of the lab, contributes insights to support Project Medeis.&lt;SEP&gt;A research facility serving as a cornerstone of Zastama Industries' innovation efforts, particularly in the field of warehouse automation.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-056-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-058-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-069-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-074-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-105-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-108-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-111-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-116-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-056&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-058&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-069&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-074&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-105&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-108&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-111&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-116</data>
      <data key="d5">1793666974</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Project Binroine">
      <data key="d0">Project Binroine</data>
      <data key="d1">project</data>
      <data key="d2">Project Binroine is a project managed by the Somhoine Risk Office and explores similar data dimensions to Project Medeis. It uses a risk modeling approach that may offer useful parallels for telemetry modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;An initiative in the final stages of its pilot phase, aimed at optimizing internal risk assessment workflows and being reviewed for broader implementation across departments.&lt;SEP&gt;An initiative currently under risk assessment by the Somhoine Risk Office. It is managed independently and focuses on identifying and addressing potential challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategic initiative with an approved budget of $6.1M, progressing according to schedule and being developed on the Garelor Relay.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-072-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-102-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-113-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-072&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-102&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-113</data>
      <data key="d5">1793666835</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Somhoine Risk Office">
      <data key="d0">Somhoine Risk Office</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Somhoine Risk Office is an organization that manages Project Binroine and applies risk modeling techniques. Their approach is being considered for potential synergies with Project Medeis.&lt;SEP&gt;An internal office at Zastama Industries responsible for identifying, mitigating, and managing enterprise-wide risks.&lt;SEP&gt;A department overseeing Project Binroine and managing enterprise-wide risk criteria, playing a central role in internal risk assessments and strategic alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;A department or office responsible for risk management and providing updates on the warehouse automation project.&lt;SEP&gt;The organization responsible for risk oversight, particularly for Project Binroine. It is tasked with identifying and addressing potential challenges proactively.&lt;SEP&gt;An office responsible for overseeing the technical and logistical complexities of strategic projects, including Project Binroine and Project Drosvais.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-054-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-072-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-096-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-102-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-113-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-054&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-072&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-096&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-102&lt;SEP&gt;d-public-113</data>
      <data key="d5">1793666835</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-Functional Steering Committee">
      <data key="d0">Cross-Functional Steering Committee</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Cross-Functional Steering Committee is a group involved in overseeing and guiding the implementation of Project Medeis. They are being updated on budget mapping and cost efficiency opportunities.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042</data>
      <data key="d5">1793658118</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="$2.7M Budget">
      <data key="d0">$2.7M Budget</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The $2.7M Budget is the approved financial allocation for Project Medeis. It is being mapped and analyzed to identify cost efficiencies and reallocation opportunities.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042</data>
      <data key="d5">1793658118</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maintenance Downtime">
      <data key="d0">Maintenance Downtime</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maintenance downtime refers to the time when equipment or vehicles are out of service due to maintenance. Research has identified correlations between fleet telemetry and this downtime, which is relevant to Project Medeis.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042</data>
      <data key="d5">1793658118</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Data Patterns">
      <data key="d0">Data Patterns</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Data patterns are recurring structures or trends in data that can inform modeling and decision-making. Krodaor Thaborine has identified data patterns that are valuable for Project Medeis.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042</data>
      <data key="d5">1793658118</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Telemetry Modeling">
      <data key="d0">Telemetry Modeling</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Telemetry modeling involves using telemetry data to create predictive models. It is a key activity in Project Medeis and is being informed by insights from the Daslaor Applied Research Lab.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-042-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">d-public-042</data>
      <data key="d5">1793658118</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cost Efficiencies">
      <data key="d0">Cost Efficiencies</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cost efficiencies refer to ways of reducing expenses while maintaining or improving performance. The Cross-Functional Steering Committee is exploring how insights from telemetry and other projects can lead to cost efficiencies in Project Medeis.&lt;SEP&gt;Strategies being explored to maintain financial control without compromising the delivery timelines of Project Komsonor.</data>
