    <node id="Reporting Structure">
      <data key="d0">Reporting Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reporting Structure refers to the hierarchical framework that defines roles, responsibilities, and accountability within teams. A clearer reporting structure was identified as necessary to improve efficiency and response times.&lt;SEP&gt;The hierarchical framework for communication and accountability, which Nogem Lorgaett was asked to provide feedback on by October 20, 2024.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reporting Structure refers to the hierarchical framework within Zastama Industries that defines who Losmais Zoslesine reports to and how her performance and access permissions are managed.&lt;SEP&gt;Reporting Structure refers to the hierarchical arrangement of team members, with Zondila Krerraris reporting directly to Thuszus Kustoen and providing updates to the finance representative.&lt;SEP&gt;The hierarchical relationships and communication lines within the Donnoett Loom product team, which were confirmed and proposed for review.</data>
