    <node id="Security Team">
      <data key="d0">Security Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Security Team is an internal group within Zastama Industries responsible for managing and overseeing a wide range of security-related functions across various projects and company-wide operations. Their primary responsibilities include managing access protocols, issuing and auditing access badges, and ensuring all credentials are valid and compliant with established security policies. The team conducts company-wide audits of access controls and confirms compliance with current standards for key and badge systems, such as the vault key ID LP-3408-A.

The Security Team plays a critical role in customer onboarding by implementing authentication protocols and ensuring that access privileges are assigned based on the principle of least privilege. They collaborate with the finance team to verify that access levels align with job responsibilities and reflect the minimum necessary for required duties. The team is also tasked with approving changes to access levels for personnel, particularly in projects such as Project Lathonel. Additionally, they maintain the integrity of high-priority sites and projects, including Project Ruzonine and Project Zasmemine. They assess whether access badge systems for one project, such as Project Zothoris, require integration with another, like Project Tosven, and ensure such decisions align with broader security strategies. Their work spans multiple initiatives, including Project Brasti, where they focus specifically on badge and key control policies.

The Security Team is also responsible for managing and streamlining access control processes for the Femfasel Vault and the Sabrinett Analytics Unit. They review access logs, verify access protocols, and ensure compliance with internal security standards. The team supports system-wide security enhancements and facilitates the transition to new access badge standards. In addition, they are tasked with reviewing and managing access credentials and protocols, including confirming the status of access badge series such as GK-9160-P and associated clearance levels for individuals like Pedusel Ruloett.</data>
      <data key="d3">d-public-111-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-020-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-027-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_a-048-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-000-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-015-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-019-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-team_b-022-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-010-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-016-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-018-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-028-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-035-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;d-exec-046-chunk-000</data>
